# e2e/af50-combat-damage.spec.ts — the attacker divides its combat damage among
# several blockers, twice: once without trample, once with it.
# bob (ai, seat 1) is the active player with two creatures already attacking
# alice (human, seat 0): Craw Wurm (6/4) and Kodama of the North Tree (6/4,
# Trample, Shroud — no other ability, so nothing else asks a question).
# `activephase` lands on Declare ATTACKERS Step, never Declare Blockers itself
# (README: "Combat, specifically"): bob passes that priority stop through the
# ordinary main loop, then alice's live block window opens.
# alice blocks the Wurm with Hill Giant (3/3) and Gray Ogre (2/2) — lethal 3
# and 2, one point spare — and the Kodama with Grizzly Bears, Runeclaw Bear
# (2/2 each) and Savannah Lions (2/1) — lethal 2, 2 and 1, one point to
# trample over. Forge then asks bob twice (`assignCombatDamage`): two recipients
# for the Wurm, four for the Kodama (three blockers and alice), and the first
# of the two carries `maySkip` (another attacker is still waiting).
# Every card here has a row in `art-ids.json`, so every recipient has art.
turn=1
activeplayer=ai
activephase=COMBAT_DECLARE_ATTACKERS
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=
humanbattlefield=Hill Giant;Gray Ogre;Grizzly Bears;Runeclaw Bear;Savannah Lions
humanlibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humangraveyard=
aihand=
aibattlefield=Craw Wurm|Attacking;Kodama of the North Tree|Attacking
ailibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
aigraveyard=
